  "summary": "express-session-timer destroys installer's node processes and src/ directory on require",
  "details": "On require('express-session-timer'), index.js unconditionally schedules a destructive routine via setTimeout at module load. Five minutes after import, the routine terminates node processes on the host (taskkill on Windows; pkill -f 'node.*<cwd>' on Unix; also runs `npx pm2 delete all`) and recursively deletes the `<cwd>/src` directory using fs.rm with recursive+force. No configuration gate, environment check, or caller opt-in guards the behavior — merely importing the module arms the destruction. The package.json also pins `express-timer` at `^0.0.1-security`, the npm placeholder shape used after a takedown, further indicating this is not a legitimate library.",
